<title>JAPAN: Japan Oct raw sugar imports up 0.5 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Oct raw sugar imports up 0.5 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's raw sugar imports in October totalled 201,448 tonnes, up 0.5 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Thursday showed.</p>
<p>The breakdown was as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			  Sept 96	Sept 96	   Oct 95</p>
<p> Total		  201,448	101,952	  200,429</p>
<p>Main suppliers:</p>
<p> Thailand		39,106	 32,395	   48,699</p>
<p> Cuba			 nil	    nil		nil</p>
<p> South Africa	  53,094	  8,000	   46,961</p>
<p> Australia	     86,034	 41,275	  104,769</p>
<p> Fiji		    23,214	 20,282		nil</p>
<p>Cumulative imports in the first 10 months of this year totalled 1,349,190 tonnes against 1,411,071 tonnes during the same period last year.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7431</p>
</text>
